{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790331441,"nonce":"IaWP24Jomb/UWuiMtYHz19WcuHg=","title":"Lua: strings lose identity under %p, gsub and long constants","message":"Strings lose identity. Boxing a typed Str copies it, so %p differs between calls. Equal short strings are not canonical under %p. Equal long literal constants in a chunk are not one object. gsub returns a new string even when nothing changed. The copies also double collectgarbage('count') for boxed large strings.\n\nWhere the official 5.4.9 suite stops on it: strings.lua:189; pm.lua:413,416,426; literals.lua:225-228; gc.lua:463 (accidental),465 (count part).\n\nSubsystem: value representation (strings) + library (gsub, %p). Plan root cause RC-string-identity, package LO-string-identity.","files":null}]}